d 'XDTREE': module to display a directory's structure in a tree-like format
d
d  xdtree displays directory contents as a text tree in Stata's
d Results window. It supports recursive traversal, a configurable
d depth limit, and filename filtering using wildcard patterns or
d regular expressions, with options to invert matches and ignore
d case. Users can also request that the directory be opened in the
d operating system's file browser. The command can be used
d independently or by xproj to inspect a project's directory
d structure. This utility was previously distributed on my personal
d site under the name dirtree. It has been renamed to avoid
d conflict with Maarten Buis's SSC package of that name. It is not
d an update to, or a replacement for, his package. 
d
d KW: directory
d KW: tree
d KW: workflow
d
d Requires: Stata version 14
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261116
d
d Author: Yongyi Zeng,  School of Management, Xiamen University, China
